<title>USA: IPO PRICING - Titan prices at $11.</title>
<headline>IPO PRICING - Titan prices at $11.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name	    Titan Exploration Inc</p>
<p>   Priced At					 $11</p>
<p>   Estimated Pricing Range	   $9.50 - $11.50</p>
<p>   Number of Shares		     12,610,000</p>
<p>   Lead Underwriter		CS First Boston</p>
<p>NOTE: The Midland, Texas company is an independent energy company engaged in the exploration, development and acquisition of oil and gas properties.</p>
<p>Of the total number of shares, 12.5 million are being sold by the company and 110,000 are being sold by selling shareholder First Union Corp.</p>
<p>Co-underwriters are Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette, Howard Weil Labouisse Friedrichs Inc, JP Morgan &amp; Co and Petrie Parkman &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Titan said it plans to use proceeds for repayment of debt incurred in connection with the acquisition of additional Permian Basin producing properties.</p>
</text>
